LESSONS["3D"].mainReading=[{"title": "World Records", "topic": "Popular videos, longest, most dangerous, oldest", "text": "WHAT WAS MORE POPULAR?\nA family video uploaded online showing a baby biting his older brother's finger, or a popular video war game?\n\n\"Charlie bit my finger\" made the record books as the most liked video in one year with 908,668 \"likes.\" The video war game, however, sold 6.5 million copies in the first 24 hours of its launch in the United States and UK alone.\n\nWHAT'S THE LONGEST?\nThe longest snake in the world, the shortest street, or the world record for the long jump?\n\nThe world's longest snake, a python, is 7.67 meters (25 feet 2 inches) long. It's the scariest inhabitant at a haunted house attraction in Kansas City, Missouri.\n\nMeanwhile, the shortest street in the world, in Caithness, Scotland, is only 2 meters (6 feet 9 inches) long. It consists of one house with the address 1, Ebenezer Place.\n\nThe world record for the long jump was set in 1991. Mike Powell from the United States jumped 8.95 meters (29 feet 4.36 inches) in Tokyo, Japan. More than two decades later, it was still the world record.\n\nWHICH IS MORE DANGEROUS?\nThe most dangerous road in the world, or the most dangerous animal?\n\nThe most dangerous road in the world runs 69 kilometers (43 miles) from La Paz to Coroico in Bolivia. On average there are 300 deaths annually. The road is most dangerous in the rainy season when it is muddy and wet.\n\nThe deadliest animal is the mosquito. This tiny insect can carry a deadly disease, malaria. Malaria kills more than two million people a year.\n\nWHICH IS OLDER?\nThe oldest skyscraper city, or the oldest living tree?\n\nThe oldest skyscraper city in the world is in Yemen. Shibam, with approximately 7,000 citizens, has buildings up to 12 stories high. While they are not the tallest skyscrapers in the world (the tallest is currently in Dubai, UAE), they are the oldest. Most of the 500 skyscrapers were built in the sixteenth century. However, Hong Kong, the place with the most skyscrapers, has 2,354 towering buildings, which together would almost reach a space station orbiting Earth.\n\nSome of the oldest forests in the world are in the Andes, a mountain range in southern Chile and Argentina. The average age of these forests is 2,500 years old. However, the oldest living tree, a pine tree in the White Mountains of California, is 4,800 years old.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["launch", "inhabitant", "consists of", "annually", "citizens", "towering"], "gist": {"q": "What is this article mainly about?", "o": ["A set of surprising world records on different topics", "A guide to the best places to visit in the world", "The history of video games"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, "detailed": [{"q": "Did the most popular video war game sell 6.5 million copies in one day or one month?", "o": ["One day (in the first 24 hours)", "One month"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Is the longest snake shorter or longer than the world's longest long jump?", "o": ["Shorter than the long jump record (7.67 m vs. 8.95 m)", "Longer than the long jump record"], "a": 0, "ex": "مار ۷.۶۷ متر است و رکورد پرش طول ۸.۹۵ متر — پس مار کوتاه‌تر است."}, {"q": "Do the people at 1, Ebenezer Place have any next-door neighbors?", "o": ["No — it's the only house on the street", "Yes, several neighbors"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "When is the worst time for accidents on the dangerous road in Bolivia?", "o": ["During the wet, rainy season", "During the cold season"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which city has the most skyscrapers — Shibam, Dubai, or Hong Kong?", "o": ["Hong Kong", "Shibam", "Dubai"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Is the oldest living tree located in one of the oldest forests (the Andes)?", "o": ["No — it's in the White Mountains of California, a different place", "Yes, it's in the Andes"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]}];
LESSONS["3D"].writingTask={"title": "An interesting place in your country", "text": "Write a short article (100–150 words) about an interesting place in your country — a mountain, a building, a natural feature, or a record-holder of some kind. Use at least one superlative, and add extra information using the apposition pattern from the Help note (Noun, extra info, ...)."};
LESSONS["3D"].grammar={vocabInContext:[{"q": "After a launch, a company starts to _____ a product.", "o": ["sell", "design"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "An inhabitant is a thing or person that _____ a place.", "o": ["lives in", "visits"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "If a street consists of one house, it means it _____ one house.", "o": ["has", "is famous for"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "When something happens annually, it happens every _____.", "o": ["year", "month"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A city that has 7,000 citizens has 7,000 _____.", "o": ["people", "buildings"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A towering building is very _____.", "o": ["tall", "short"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]};
LESSONS["3D"].sessions=[{"id": "cb1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "🔎", "title": "Scan first", "fa": "ابتدا مرور سریع کنید", "parts": [{"t": "scanpre", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📖", "title": "Reading", "fa": "متن کامل", "parts": [{"t": "fullread", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Comprehension", "fa": "درک مطلب", "parts": [{"t": "comprehension", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "🔤", "title": "Vocabulary in context", "fa": "واژگان در متن", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "vocabInContext", "label": "Vocabulary in context"}]}, {"id": "cb5", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "Sample", "fa": "نمونه‌ی نوشتاری", "parts": [{"t": "writingSample", "title": "Mount Aconcagua", "text": "MOUNT ACONCAGUA — THE HIGHEST MOUNTAIN IN ARGENTINA\n\nMount Aconcagua, a peak in the Andes range, is the highest mountain in Argentina. At 6,962 meters (22,841 feet), it is the highest mountain in North and South America. Many people come to Argentina every year to climb Mount Aconcagua and to see the Andes, the longest mountain range in the world."}]}, {"id": "cb6", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "💡", "title": "Writing Tips", "fa": "نکات نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writingPoints", "title": "Adding information", "html": "<h3>اضافه کردن اطلاعات (Apposition)</h3>\n<p>می‌توانید با قرار دادن یک عبارت توصیفی بلافاصله بعد از اسم (بین دو کاما)، اطلاعات بیشتری به جمله اضافه کنید — بدون نوشتن یک جمله‌ی جداگانه.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">Mount Aconcagua is the highest mountain in Argentina. + It is a peak in the Andes range. → <b>Mount Aconcagua, a peak in the Andes range, is the highest mountain in Argentina.</b></div>\n<div class=\"ex\">Many people come to see the Andes. + They are the longest mountain range in the world. → <b>Many people come to see the Andes, the longest mountain range in the world.</b></div>"}]}, {"id": "cb7", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Write about an interesting place", "fa": "درباره‌ی یک مکان جالب بنویسید", "parts": [{"t": "writing", "key": "taskOnly"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];

